FREELANCE USE: FREELANCE LICENSE

A Freelance license permits one named individual to use this software
for commercial purposes in that individual's own freelance work and
side projects, including work for the individual's own clients and the
individual's own commercial apps, provided the individual's total
income from that work and those projects was under US $10,000 in the
preceding 12 months. Holding other employment does not prevent an
individual from using a Freelance license.

A Freelance license does not cover work the individual performs for an
employer, or use within any organization's internal systems, products
or operations. That use requires a Builder, Studio or Platform license.

When the individual's income from that work and those projects reaches
US $10,000 in any 12-month period, continued commercial use requires a
Builder or higher license. The amount paid for the Freelance license
counts toward it.

